<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins 160 mln skr Japan deal.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins 160 mln skr Japan deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB said on Monday it had won an order worth 160 million crowns to extend the Japanese Digital Tuka Hokkaido's PDC standard mobile phone system.</p>
<p>The order incorporates equipment for AXE standard digital exchanges and radio base stations, as well as new functions for subscribers and operators, Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The extension will give the system better coverage and increase its capacity to meet the expected subscriber growth in the (Hokkaido) area,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
